# Normalise line endings on commit, and pin the files where the ending is not
# cosmetic.
#
# The shell scripts and Dockerfiles matter: a CRLF `start.sh` cloned onto Linux
# fails with `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`, and a CRLF line inside a Dockerfile
# RUN becomes part of the command. Windows checkouts get CRLF for the rest, so
# editors here behave normally.
* text=auto

*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF — it is only ever run on Windows.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary: keep git from "normalising" these into corruption.
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.zst   binary
*.tar   binary
